WEBVTT

00:07:28.709 --> 00:07:31.390
LOL is being used in a very particular way.

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:35.081
It's a marker of empathy. It's a marker of accommodation.

00:07:35.081 --> 00:07:38.330
We linguists call things like that pragmatic particles.

00:07:38.330 --> 00:07:42.169
Any spoken language that's used by real people has them.

00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:43.945
If you happen to speak Japanese, think about

00:07:43.945 --> 00:07:47.303
that little word "ne" that you use at the end of a lot of sentences.

00:07:47.303 --> 00:07:49.648
If you listen to the way black youth today speak,

00:07:49.648 --> 00:07:51.434
think about the use of the word "yo."

00:07:51.434 --> 00:07:53.380
Whole dissertations could be written about it,

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:55.654
and probably are being written about it.

00:07:55.654 --> 00:07:59.448
A pragmatic particle, that's what LOL has gradually become.

00:07:59.448 --> 00:08:03.497
It's a way of using the language between actual people.